# Tests

There are jest tests that test logic that does not need a browser. Every test that need a browser are run by vitest.

# run server tests

Use test explorer of vscode (View -> Testing) to run and debug the tests. Actually there is a Problem with debugging vs-code if the vitest plugin ist installed. Somehow it changes the NODE_OPTIONS or similar stuff so that debugging of node server does no longer work. Breakpoints will not hit.

# run browser tests

start test server via launch config:
```json
{
  "name": "testserver.js",
  "type": "node",
  "request": "launch",
  "program": "${workspaceFolder}/_src/tests/test-server/dst/tests/test-server/testserver.js",
  "cwd": "${workspaceFolder}/_src/tests/test-server/dst/tests/test-server",
  "runtimeExecutable": "${env:HOME}/.nvm/versions/node/v22.16.0/bin/node",
  "console": "integratedTerminal"
},
```
So you can set breakpoints for the server side in vscode.

Install "vitest.explorer" extension in vscode. than use the vscode test explorer (View -> Testing) to run  and debug the tests.